-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem">Common Questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can you short-term rental in Garden City Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Generally yes. Garden City is unincorporated, so there is no city STR ban; properties follow Horry County (or Georgetown County) rules plus any HOA or condo-regime restrictions. You still collect and remit accommodations tax.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Garden City in Horry or Georgetown County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Mostly Horry County, with a southern tip in Georgetown County near the inlet. The county can affect taxes and school assignment, and Chapter3 will confirm this by address.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What kind of property is Garden City known for?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Oceanfront and ocean-view condos along Waccamaw Drive and raised beach houses, with a strong vacation-rental market anchored by the Garden City Pier.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What are property taxes on a second home in Garden City?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A primary home is taxed on 4 percent of its value and does not pay the school operating tax. A second home is taxed on 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. In Garden City that makes a second home's bill about 3.2 times a primary home's on the same house.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Which schools serve Garden City?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Horry-side properties are generally served by Seaside Elementary, St. James Middle, and St. James High in Horry County Schools; the Georgetown-side tip is served by the Georgetown County School District. Confirm by address.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Garden City good for vacation rentals?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes, it is a popular vacation-rental area, with both oceanfront and marsh-side property creating a range of price points.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Where is Garden City located?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">On a narrow stretch between Myrtle Beach and Murrells Inlet, with ocean on one side and marsh on the other.</p></div></div></section>
