+    { h2: "What is there to do in Garden City, SC?", toc: "Things to do", id: "things-to-do", html: () =>
+      h.p(`A summer day here starts on the beach and ends on the pier. For dinner, the ${h.ext(MARSHWALK, "MarshWalk")} in Murrells Inlet is about ${D.marshwalk} minutes away by car. It is a half-mile wooden boardwalk along the marsh, lined with restaurants such as Drunken Jack's, Dead Dog Saloon, Creek Ratz and The Wicked Tuna, and its live music is free to hear.`) +
+      h.p(`For a day out, ${h.ext(HBSP, "Huntington Beach State Park")} is 15 to 20 minutes south. It has 3 miles of beach, a freshwater lake where you are almost sure to see alligators, and bird-watching the state calls some of the best on the East Coast. Atalaya, the winter home of Archer and Anna Hyatt Huntington, stands in the park, and Brookgreen Gardens is next to it.`) +
+      h.p(`For groceries, Kroger on Business 17 is about ${GD.kroger} minutes from the pier by car, and the Walmart Supercenter on the Garden City Connector about ${GD.walmart}.`) +
